  "term": "drug interactions",
  "definition": "Drug interactions are effects that can occur when two drugs are used together, potentially changing how well treatment works or affecting safety. In the source context, this is especially relevant in polypharmacy, such as combining cardiovascular medicines with antidepressants, where co-medication may create risks.",
